cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fortran_shapefuncs: Finite element shape functions, including mapped infinite elements"
type: software
abstract: >-
  fortran_shapefuncs is a Fortran module, shapefuncs, with the derived type
  shapefunc: the shape functions of a finite element and their first and
  second derivatives at the points of a cubature from fortran_cubatures.
  It covers lines, triangles, quadrilaterals, tetrahedra, hexahedra and
  wedges of any order, serendipity quadrilaterals and hexahedra of orders 1
  to 3, and the mapped infinite elements of Zienkiewicz, Emson and Bettess.
  Nodes are numbered hierarchically, and the caller can permute the
  numbering. Every element is checked by function-space reproduction tests.
  It is Fortran 2018 and builds with fpm or make.
authors:
